model {
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "A provider HTTP submission whose write or response was observed cannot be replayed after transport loss or an empty accepted stream, including internal HTTP, model, credential and retry-round fallbacks. The final selected transport records request-local evidence without replacing proxy, TLS or pool policy. Before output starts, ambiguous outcomes return 502 upstream_outcome_unknown with retryable false and x-should-retry false. Late protocol truncation retains partial output and emits an outcome-unknown error without inventing completion. Safe pre-write connection failures and explicit HTTP refusals retain retry behavior. Real loopback regressions guard both the public API and transport replay before the native source image is built. Publication still requires the actual source and compiled producers to agree on an exact reviewed serving-to-candidate source pair, preserving the existing native schema version and complete index registry. Keep the carry until an upstream release passes the same behavior, re-applying it across source updates without rolling back the release pin."
    }
  }
}
